      "record": "21-25",
      "detail": "3rd in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Two straight wins have given the Blue Jays a little oxygen, and they needed it. <strong>Sunday's 4-1 takedown of the Tigers</strong> was the kind of tidy, no-nonsense victory a club stranded at 21-25 and sitting 3rd in the AL East can use as a brake and a spark at once. The Jays are still nine and a half back, so nobody is mistaking this for a charge, but the swing of the week has been real - after dropping a 3-2 squeaker on Friday, they answered with a 2-1 grinder on Saturday and then handled business yesterday. That's the difference between drifting and hanging around. The bats haven't exactly roared, but they've done enough, and the pitching has kept the train on the tracks. Now comes the real measuring stick: a Monday night date with the Yankees in New York, the sort of game that tells you whether this bounce is a blip or the first sign of life. <strong>Watch whether the Jays can turn this two-game burst into something sturdier at Yankee Stadium.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 18, 2026"
      },
