      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The draft is in the books, and now comes the hard part - turning optimism into Sundays that matter. Washington sits 3rd in the NFC East at 6 games back, with a lonely W1 tag on the ledger and the blunt truth of a 14th playoff seed hanging over it; that's not contention, that's a reminder that the roster still needs weight, speed and sturdier hands in the right places. <strong>The real news is the rookie class the Commanders just brought in, headlined by linebacker Sonny Styles and the rest of a haul meant to shore up a defense that too often bent like wet cardboard.</strong> The offense, meanwhile, still leans on Terry McLaurin and a run game that now has Rachaad White in the picture, but the bigger question is whether the new additions can supply the second and third layer this team has lacked. Jayden Daniels' health remains the franchise's pulse; if he's upright, everything else has a chance to breathe. <strong>For now, the eye goes to how quickly the rookies crack the depth chart when camps open.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 18, 2026"
      },
